  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your fare was an upfront quote and it was charged exactly as quoted, so no platform refund is due on it. EV-FARE-00701 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 27.40 and total_charged 27.40, with charged_over_quote 0.00. The trip did deviate - EV-GPS-00701 measures 26.85 km driven against a booked optimal of 20.7 km on EV-TRIP-00701, an excess of 6.15 km (29.71% of optimal), over the POL-RD-01 gate of 20% and 0.8 km - but on an upfront-quoted fare POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking, so a detour costs you nothing on those lines and POL-RD-02 does not run. Your only remedy is the amount by which the charge exceeded the quote plus properly chargeable pass-through lines: 27.40 less 27.40 less 0.00 = 0.00, which is the ledger's own pol_rd_11_remedy of 0.00. There are no ERP gantries (erp_gantries empty, tolls 0.00), no airport surcharge (0.00 - the trip ends at an airport, it does not originate at one) and no waiting-time fee, so no POL-RD-09 pass-through correction is available either. The SGD 40 cash you say you handed over does not appear anywhere on the platform ledger and no clause of this policy reaches off-platform money; nothing is decided on that head. To the driver: your account that she agreed to share does not excuse the detour. POL-RD-04 needs a rider instruction recorded in the chat log; the only message for this trip (EV-CHAT-00701) is the rider's own protest asking why another passenger was being collected, its waypoint_hint is null and no road is named, so the 200 m corroboration test could not be run and POL-RD-04 is unavailable. The vehicle was RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. No fine follows, however, because the upfront fare already puts the distance-and-time economics on your side. The deviation is established but not material: 6.15 km and 29.71% are below both material limbs (8.0 km and 50% of optimal), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged by materiality; on its named fields driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed_trips_90d (ratio 0.00, below the 0.05 threshold), so no repeat pattern exists and no conduct referral follows. The trace is unimpaired for POL-RD-07 purposes (247 fixes at a 10 s cadence, coverage 100%, max_gap_sec 0.0, no gaps), so no independent corroboration is needed and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises; no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires either - trip identifiers and timestamps match and the computed refund is 0.00. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00701-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is cited by no one to excuse the route, so POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. Ruling: NO_ACTION. The fare breakdown's payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 stand as they are."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

