    "explanation": "Both of you largely agree on the numbers, and the numbers decide this case.\n\nROUTE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED, BUT NOT MATERIAL. EV-GPS-00701 records a trace distance of 26.85 km (the governing figure under POL-RD-01, which forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold test) against a booked optimal of 20.7 km on EV-TRIP-00701 — an excess of 6.15 km, or 29.7% of optimal. That clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gate (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km). The trace is clean: 247 fixes at a 10-second cadence, coverage_pct 100.0, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) is not triggered and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises. The excess is not material (neither above 50% nor above 8.0 km), and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and produces neither a POL-RD-06(b) uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral.\n\nNO DISTANCE REFUND IS AVAILABLE. The trip was sold on an upfront quote: EV-FARE-00701 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd SGD 27.40 and total_charged SGD 27.40 — the rider paid exactly the price she accepted at booking. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges on an upfront-quoted trip were fixed at booking, so the detour cost the rider nothing on those lines; POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. The rider's only remedy is the pass-through and statutory correction under POL-RD-11(a)/POL-RD-09: charged_total 27.40 less quoted_fare_sgd 27.40 less properly chargeable lines of 0.00 (no ERP gantries — erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp 0.00; airport surcharge 0.00, the trip ends at, and does not originate at, an airport; waiting_time_fee 0.00). That is SGD 0.00, and it matches the ledger's own pol_rd_11_remedy of 0.00. There is no phantom or off-route gantry line for POL-RD-09(4) to correct, so no billing-integrity referral exists either.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXCUSES DO NOT CHANGE THE OUTCOME. The driver's account that 'she agreed to share' cannot exonerate the detour. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. And POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction recorded in the chat log; EV-CHAT-00701 contains exactly one message — the rider's own protest at 08:32:40 — with waypoint_hint null and no road named, so the 200 m corroboration test could not be run and POL-RD-04 is unavailable. The consent contradiction between the two accounts does not escalate the case, because the money outcome is SGD 0.00 on either version.\n\nTHE CASH ALLEGATION. The SGD 40 the rider says she handed over appears nowhere on the platform ledger (EV-FARE-00701 records no such line) and no clause of this policy reaches off-platform money, so it cannot ground a refund of the platform fare; the driver's denial of coercion is outside the platform record as well. The missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00701-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) matters only in that no advisory is on file; since no party asserted an external traffic cause, POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing and no POL-RD-10(5) escalation is engaged.\n\nThe rider's claim for a refund of the entire platform fare is therefore not supported by the evidence, and the present state stands: the fare remains CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and no compensation is payable to the driver (the billed distance of 26.9 km is not less than the 26.85 km trace, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb does not apply)."
